{"id": "EUVD-2026-76282", "enisaUuid": "d6beddc7-dec4-336d-8e90-5c81f23716d7", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndm-pcache: bound the persisted tail-position offset\n\ncache_pos_decode() takes the persisted key_tail and dirty_tail seg_off from\nthe cache device and addresses within the segment with it. A seg_off at or\npast the segment data_size, controllable by whoever supplies the device\n(CAP_SYS_ADMIN), reads past the segment data.\n\nReject a decoded seg_off that is not below the segment data_size.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:42:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:45:43", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ffd9a214a94f9928e54856f42b1cc3e33fb10e36", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8bf7a06ca3c1611809725f58cfd573f2ffbda75f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d1898576090a10d2ac2715218a652e78fb65a6b0"], "aliases": ["GHSA-9gr7-7h3r-cj7p", "CVE-2026-80959"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3a582499-6dfb-3e44-80d2-26d1c1e3c362", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1d57628ff95b32d5cfa8d8f50e07690c161e9cf0 <d1898576090a10d2ac2715218a652e78fb65a6b0"}, {"id": "41fe7795-f1ed-3a3e-8165-0703aef53229", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1d57628ff95b32d5cfa8d8f50e07690c161e9cf0 <ffd9a214a94f9928e54856f42b1cc3e33fb10e36"}, {"id": "624ec472-3371-35b8-889d-54ae317d01d8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18"}, {"id": "666519ea-7dc8-3d81-a7a2-9b2048af1792", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1d57628ff95b32d5cfa8d8f50e07690c161e9cf0 <8bf7a06ca3c1611809725f58cfd573f2ffbda75f"}, {"id": "706df749-80b6-33ac-b396-28768e6f1e13", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version":